                                "sense_id": "afbaae99-82e6-3b8c-a122-e3729189a675",
                                "text": "As I have shown, “bad” affective modes such as humor, irony, sardonicism, self-reflexivity, satire, and irreverence allow them to confront enduring legacies around Native American and African American relationships to the environment, especially racialized environmental affect, and to critique readerly and other public expectations."
